    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Change a whole local audio file's playback speed and create a new file.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --input TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Input media file path.\r\n          --output TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Output media file path.\r\n          --speed FLOAT:POSITIVE REQUIRED \r\n                              Absolute playback-speed multiplier; must be finite and positive.\r\n          --preserve-pitch Excludes: --no-preserve-pitch \r\n                              Keep the original audio pitch while changing duration (default).\r\n          --no-preserve-pitch Excludes: --preserve-pitch \r\n                              Allow pitch to change with playback speed.\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  $ lyra-cli media change-audio-speed --input /tmp/in.m4a --output /tmp/out.m4a --speed 1.5 --preserve-pitch\r\nNOTES\r\n  If encoded output duration drifts by more than 100ms, the output is deleted and the command fails.\r\n",
